      "rev_n_8_289730_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_8_289730_0",
        "node_id": "n_8_289730",
        "thought_text": "Use a combinatorial approach: calculate the total number of intersection points formed by the arrangement of lines and subtract cases where multiple lines intersect at the same point (overcounting), though this might be complex due to the 'single common wire' rule for collinear points.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-2570079942259561846",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794590228.1418474
      },
      "rev_n_9_f68076_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_9_f68076_0",
        "node_id": "n_9_f68076",
        "thought_text": "Since n is very small (50), implement a brute-force O(L^2) check where L is the number of unique lines (at most C(n,2)), using cross-product logic to determine if two lines intersect at a unique point within the plane.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-2570079942259561846",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794590228.141855
      },
      "rev_n_10_c54a62_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_10_c54a62_0",
        "node_id": "n_10_c54a62",
        "thought_text": "Iterate through all unique lines formed by the points (merging collinear points), then use a nested loop to count pairs of lines that are not parallel by checking the cross product of their normal vectors.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-5733110888159023883",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794590285.6732938
      },
      "rev_n_11_dd099e_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_11_dd099e_0",
        "node_id": "n_11_dd099e",
        "thought_text": "Represent each line using integer coefficients (A, B, C) derived from the cross product of point differences, store unique lines in a set, and count intersections by verifying $A_1B_2 - A_2B_1 \\neq 0$.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-5733110888159023883",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
